<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="description" content="Bind is a whole-application language that verifies client, server, environment, and database boundaries before your application builds.">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#efeee8">
    <meta property="og:title" content="Bind — If it does not bind, it does not build.">
    <meta property="og:description" content="Bind is a whole-application language that verifies client, server, environment, and database boundaries before your application builds.">
    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <title>Bind — If it does not bind, it does not build.</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 64 64'%3E%3Crect width='64' height='64' fill='%2311130f'/%3E%3Ctext x='32' y='45' text-anchor='middle' font-family='monospace' font-size='40' font-weight='700' fill='%23c8ff36'%3EB%3C/text%3E%3C/svg%3E">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="bind-site"><div class="page"><header class="site-header"><nav class="nav wrap"><a href="#top" class="brand"><span class="brand-mark">B</span><span class="brand-name">bind</span></a><div class="nav-links"><a href="#language" class="nav-link">Language</a><a href="#proof" class="nav-link">Guarantees</a><a href="https://github.com/bind-lang/bind" class="nav-link external" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a></div><a href="https://github.com/bind-lang/bind" class="nav-cta" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the source</a></nav></header><main class="main"><section class="hero wrap" id="top"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot">●</span>WHOLE-APPLICATION LANGUAGE / 0.1</p><h1 class="hero-title">One language.
Every boundary.</h1><p class="hero-intro">Bind sees the client, server, environment, and database as one typed application — then proves they agree before anything ships.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a href="https://github.com/bind-lang/bind#quick-start" class="button button-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Start binding<span class="button-arrow">↗</span></a><a href="#language" class="button button-quiet">See the language<span class="button-arrow">↓</span></a></div></div><aside class="hero-graph"><div class="graph-topline"><span class="graph-kicker">VERIFIED APPLICATION GRAPH</span><span class="graph-live">LIVE</span></div><div class="graph-stage"><div class="graph-source"><span class="graph-file">commerce.bd</span><code class="graph-code">client component Shop()
server fun checkout()
entity Order(...)</code></div><div class="graph-spine"><span class="graph-pulse pulse-one"></span><span class="graph-pulse pulse-two"></span></div><div class="graph-targets"><div class="graph-target"><span class="target-index">01</span><span class="target-name">BROWSER</span><span class="target-state">BOUND</span></div><div class="graph-target"><span class="target-index">02</span><span class="target-name">SERVER</span><span class="target-state">BOUND</span></div><div class="graph-target"><span class="target-index">03</span><span class="target-name">POSTGRES</span><span class="target-state">BOUND</span></div></div></div><div class="graph-footer"><span>0 boundary mismatches</span><span>rust-web-v4</span></div></aside></section><section class="manifesto-band"><div class="band-track"><span>IF IT DOES NOT BIND, IT DOES NOT BUILD.</span><span class="band-glyph">✳</span><span>IF IT DOES NOT BIND, IT DOES NOT BUILD.</span><span class="band-glyph">✳</span><span>IF IT DOES NOT BIND, IT DOES NOT BUILD.</span></div></section><section class="language-section wrap" id="language"><div class="section-heading"><p class="section-index">01 / THE LANGUAGE</p><h2 class="section-title">The application is
the unit of truth.</h2></div><div class="language-grid"><article class="language-copy"><p class="lead">Most stacks discover integration mistakes after code crosses a boundary. Bind models those boundaries before code exists.</p><ul class="principle-list"><li class="principle"><span class="principle-number">01</span><div><h3>One typed graph</h3><p>Calls, effects, secrets, schemas, and UI bindings share the same semantic model.</p></div></li><li class="principle"><span class="principle-number">02</span><div><h3>No escape hatches</h3><p>The certified profile rejects raw SQL, target code, and untyped network calls.</p></div></li><li class="principle"><span class="principle-number">03</span><div><h3>Native output</h3><p>Verified Bind lowers to Rust, native HTML/CSS/JS, PostgreSQL contracts, and deployable platform artifacts.</p></div></li></ul></article><article class="code-window"><div class="code-header"><div class="window-dots"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div><span>customer.bd</span><span class="code-badge">BIND</span></div><pre class="code-body"><code>distinct type CustomerId = UUID

entity Customer(
    val id: CustomerId,
    val name: String,
    val email: Email
)

server fun getCustomer(id: CustomerId): Customer
    effects [db.read] {
    return db.customers.require(id)
}

client component CustomerPage(id: CustomerId) {
    val customer = server.getCustomer(id)

    UI {
        Text(customer.name)
        Text(customer.email)
    }
}</code></pre><div class="code-status"><span class="check">✓</span><span>Application bound successfully</span><span class="code-time">84ms</span></div></article></div></section><section class="proof-section" id="proof"><div class="wrap proof-wrap"><div class="section-heading proof-heading"><p class="section-index inverse">02 / BEFORE BUILD</p><h2 class="section-title inverse">Make invalid systems
impossible to ship.</h2></div><div class="proof-grid"><article class="proof-card proof-featured"><span class="proof-icon">↯</span><h3>Cross-boundary types</h3><p>Nominal and nullable types stay consistent across Bind, Rust, JSON, JavaScript, and PostgreSQL.</p><span class="proof-tag">VERIFIED</span></article><article class="proof-card"><span class="proof-icon">⌁</span><h3>Effect control</h3><p>Every database read, write, and server call is declared and checked against its deployment domain.</p><span class="proof-tag">BOUNDED</span></article><article class="proof-card"><span class="proof-icon">◇</span><h3>Secret flow</h3><p>Runtime secrets cannot leak into the browser artifact. The compiler follows the path for you.</p><span class="proof-tag">SEALED</span></article><article class="proof-card proof-wide"><div><span class="proof-icon">#</span><h3>Reproducible by construction</h3></div><p>Pinned toolchains, generated contract tests, dependency locks, and SHA-256 attestations define the exact application that passed certification.</p><span class="proof-tag">CERTIFIED-HOST</span></article></div></div></section><section class="flow-section wrap"><div class="section-heading flow-heading"><p class="section-index">03 / ONE COMMAND</p><h2 class="section-title compact">Source in.
Certainty out.</h2></div><div class="flow-line"><article class="flow-step"><span class="flow-number">01</span><h3>Parse</h3><p>Kotlin-compatible lexical surface, Bind semantics.</p></article><article class="flow-step"><span class="flow-number">02</span><h3>Verify</h3><p>Types, effects, schema, environment, and calls.</p></article><article class="flow-step"><span class="flow-number">03</span><h3>Generate</h3><p>Rust server, HTML/JS frontend, contracts, and adapters.</p></article><article class="flow-step"><span class="flow-number">04</span><h3>Certify</h3><p>Build, test, lint, optimize, lock, and attest.</p></article></div><div class="command-line"><span class="prompt">$</span><code>bind certify --target vercel</code><span class="command-result">✓ certified-host</span></div></section><section class="closing"><div class="closing-grid"><div class="closing-mark">B</div><div class="closing-copy"><p class="section-index inverse">A SMALL LANGUAGE FOR THE WHOLE SYSTEM</p><h2 class="closing-title">Stop wiring.
Start binding.</h2><p class="closing-text">Bind is early, deliberately narrow, and open source. The compiler would rather reject a program than quietly weaken its meaning.</p><a href="https://github.com/bind-lang/bind" class="button button-light" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore Bind on GitHub<span class="button-arrow">↗</span></a></div></div></section></main><footer class="footer"><div class="wrap footer-inner"><div><span class="footer-brand">bind</span><p>A whole-application language.</p></div><div class="footer-meta"><span>PROFILE / rust-web-v4</span><span>© 2026 BIND LANGUAGE</span></div></div></footer></div></div>
  </body>
</html>
